From ef9c1e5f6f6c9bbc22f0c37c083377d7c7b14894 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "wilfred.dore" <wilfred.dore@telecom-paristech.org>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 17:51:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/9] practice: replace a generator's own CSP meta with the
 application policy

A real generated activity carried its own restrictive
<meta http-equiv="Content-Security-Policy" ...>. _validate_html rejects
any CSP meta, and the prompt never said not to add one, so a sound file
was refused after download.

- The prompt now says the application adds the CSP and the file must not.
- One well-formed declaration (quoted http-equiv and content, no other
  attribute) is removed before the canonical policy is inserted and the
  full validation runs. Several, a malformed one, or any other mention of
  the header is rejected. The HTTP header and iframe sandbox are unchanged.
- validation records raw_sha256 of the downloaded bytes and the removed
  declaration; artifact_sha256 is the derived file.
- Tests: a file with its own CSP, malformed and duplicate metas, and unsafe
  HTML still rejected after removal.

Co-Authored-By: Devin AI <158243242+devin-ai-integration[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 mvp/practice.py      | 59 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++---
 mvp/test_practice.py | 47 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 102 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

